em Card:**\n   * Dynamically recommends the **first unsolved problem** in this topic (or next in sequence if solved).\n   * Displays title, LeetCode #, difficulty badge, pattern, complexity, and description.\n   * One-click **`▶ Solve & Step in Visualizer`** button that loads the code into the visualizer and starts step-by-step execution.\n4. **Topic Problem Table:**\n   * Filtered table showing all problems matching this topic.\n   * Displays **multi-topic chips** on every row so learners can see other concepts linked to the problem.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Multi-Faceted Browsing System\n\nLearners can browse, slice, and filter problems across four dimensions simultaneously:\n\n```\n[Search Keyword] + [Topic (30)] + [Difficulty (Easy/Med/Hard)] + [Algorithmic Pattern] + [Status (Solved/In-Progress/Not Started/Bookmarked)]\n```\n\n* **By Topic:** Select any of the 30 topics via the topic library or dropdown.\n* **By Difficulty:** Instant filter pills for **🟢 Easy**, **🟡 Medium**, and **🔴 Hard**.\n* **By Algorithmic Pattern:** Dropdown dynamically populated with the algorithm patterns present in the active topic or library (e.g. *Two Pointers Converging*, *Monotonic Decreasing Stack*, *Hash Map Complement*, *Prefix Sum Lookup*, *Kahn's Topological Sort*, etc.).\n* **By Learning Status:** Filter by **✅ Solved**, **⏳ In Progress / Attempted**, **⚪ Not Started**, or **⭐ Bookmarked**.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Test Audit & Verification\n\nAll test suites passed **100% with zero failures**:\n\n1. **`test_dsa_phase2.js` (34 / 34 tests passed):**\n   * Verified all 30 topic names, icons, categories, and concept summaries.\n   * Verified multi-topic tagging across all 300 problems (290 problems belong to multiple topics).\n   * Verified non-empty counts across all 30 topics.\n   * Verified difficulty distributions and recommended next problem calculation.\n   * Verified dynamic shifting of recommended problem after a problem is solved.\n   * Verified browsing by Topic, Difficulty, Algorithmic Pattern, and Learning Status.\n   * Verified dedicated topic page rendering and breadcrumb navigation.\n\n2. **`test_dsa_phase1.js` (59 / 59 tests passed):**\n   * Verified real `localStorage` tracking without fake data.\n   * Verified 300-problem library integrity.\n   * Verified execution engine runs across core problems (*Two Sum*, *Binary Search*, *Max Subarray*, *Stock*, *Container*).\n\n3. **`test_phase5.js` (82 / 82 tests passed):**\n   * Verified Kadane maximum subarray output **remains 6** on original input `[-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]`.\n   * Verified all 5 test datasets, backward/forward navigation across 197 substeps, variable addresses, prediction quiz, and speed modes.\n\n**Total Verified Tests: 175 / 175 (100% Pass).**","thinking":"The problem data and UI components are accounted for across the problem set, dashboard functionality, and styling. The problem set includes 300 problems multi-tagged with 30 topics. The dashboard component facilitates search, filtering by pattern, and displays completion progress and recommendations. The UI is styled with dedicated CSS for a 30-topic grid and details pages.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":1988,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T07:35:35Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n5. Phase 3: Create a Curated 300-Problem Library\n\nBuild a structured catalog of 300 curated DSA problems.\n\nInclude a sensible distribution across beginner, intermediate, and advanced topics. Do not force equal numbers into every category.\n\nPrioritize a learning progression:\n\nPython fundamentals and basic array operations.\n\nStrings, hashing, and frequency counting.\n\nTwo pointers and sliding windows.\n\nPrefix sums and binary search.\n\nSorting, linked lists, stacks, and queues.\n\nRecursion and backtracking.\n\nTrees, heaps, and graphs.\n\nGreedy algorithms and dynamic programming.\n\nAdvanced patterns and data structures.\n\nEach problem must have a structured record containing:\n\nUnique problem ID.\n\nProblem title.\n\nVerified source URL, preferably the official LeetCode page.\n\nDifficulty.\n\nPrimary topic.\n\nAdditional topic tags.\n\nAlgorithmic pattern.\n\nShort original problem summary.\n\nInput and output examples.\n\nConstraints, where verified.\n\nPrerequisite concepts.\n\nLearning status.\n\nBookmark status.\n\nPersonal notes.\n\nOptional Python reference solution.\n\nVerification status for the reference solution.\n\nDo not invent problem URLs, difficulty labels, constraints, or company tags.\n\nUse public, reliable sources to validate the catalog where possible. Do not claim the library is exhaustive or fully verified if it is not.\n\nDo not copy the complete copyrighted text of LeetCode problem statements. Write concise original summaries and examples, and link to the official problem page.\n\nIf 300 verified records cannot be completed in one implementation pass, create a data-driven catalog and import the remaining verified records in batches. Do not fill gaps with fake problems.\n\nThe application must remain functional when external links are unavailable.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-27T13:05:35+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
